  "question": {
    "text": "Let $0    < \\alpha < \\beta < 1$. Then $\\lim {n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\sum_{k=1}^{n} \\int_{1/k+\\beta}^{1 /(k+a)} \\frac{d x}{1+x}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\log _{e} \\frac{\\beta}{\\alpha}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\log _{e} \\frac{1+\\beta}{1+\\alpha}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\log _{e} \\frac{1+\\alpha}{1+\\beta}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\infty$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint:\r\n$\\lim _{n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\sum_{k=1}^{n}[\\log |1+x|]_{\\frac{1}{k+\\beta}} \\frac{1}{k+a}$\r\n$=\\lim _{n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\left(\\log \\left(1+\\frac{1}{k+\\alpha}\\right)-\\log \\left(1+\\frac{1}{k+\\beta}\\right)\\right)$\r\n$=\\lim _{n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\left(\\log \\left(\\frac{k+\\alpha+1}{k+\\alpha}\\right)-\\log \\left(\\frac{k+\\beta+1}{k+\\beta}\\right)\\right)$\r\n$=\\log \\left(\\frac{\\beta+1}{\\alpha+1}\\right)$"
  }
}